  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with multi-profile + avgpool (config_002, acc 0.591) is clearly the best configuration so far, outperforming single-profile RNA (0.485) and vastly outperforming image-only (0.208). Avgpool also beats transformer aggregation (0.591 vs 0.519). However, all RNA results used PCA n2000; we have no evidence about whether a learned biological representation (scvi) improves over a linear one. Question: Does replacing PCA with scvi_n200 under the same multi-profile + avgpool setup improve the RNA representation and validation accuracy? Why this is the best next experiment: config_005 changes exactly one variable (RNA encoder) relative to our best result (config_002), cleanly isolating the effect of representation while holding profile setting and aggregation fixed. This is the highest-information single experiment: if scvi helps, we know learned representations matter and should extend to scgpt and multimodal; if it doesn't, PCA is sufficient and we can pivot budget toward testing whether the weak image modality adds value in a multimodal setting. Either outcome meaningfully narrows the search space under the limited budget."
}

